1. Backport of TanStack/ai#1494 (issue #1447): a Responses stream that ends
   without a terminal event reports a RUN_ERROR with code incomplete-stream
   instead of an invented RUN_FINISHED.
   Remove when @tanstack/openai-base >= 0.12.0 is installed.
2. The terminal event carries the response's incomplete reason, or else its
   status, as metadata.providerStopReason, so the service decides every
   outcome from the SDK's unions (apps/api/src/lib/chat/provider-stop-reasons.ts).
   Remove when upstream exposes the raw reason.
3. The RUN_ERROR of an incomplete or failed response carries the response's
   usage, which it dropped. Upstream PR to be opened; remove when released.

